IVERABLE — a written scope, on this row (no code):\n             1. the surface we expose and why that surface (and, explicitly, what we do NOT expose)\n             2. the exact muster consumer block (the mcpServers entry with its real --spec path/URL\n                and --base-url) written out verbatim\n             3. the acceptance test for the later rows: the precise commands a verifier runs, and\n                the assertions that make them non-vacuous\n             4. the boundary call: which operations are agent-safe through MCP and which must be\n                gated (muster's MCP safety contract — mutating operations an agent should not\n                reach unattended)\n             5. the auth story: this service's credential/header vs what muster's config can carry\n\n             ACCEPTANCE: the row closes with the five items above present and concrete enough\n             that the spec row needs no new decision. If a real decision is still open, say so\n             and name who rules on it.","detail":{"fingerprint":"4477c3b94450238dc3da9e16e388bb912e3251cc0d960fa06a613b0e30316a3a"},"complexity":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T21:53:49.069856+00:00","capability_tags":["+integration","+protocol","+interop"],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"44fe805","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Scope doc docs/muster-protocol-scope.md landed in 44fe805 (worker d8fd31a, 469 lines): read-only muster surface (listBoards/getUploaderForm/getOpenapiSpec on a SERVED /openapi.json), POST + board writes explicitly excluded (foreman-only rule standing), verbatim mcpServers block (--spec http://127.0.0.1:8787/openapi.json), non-vacuous acceptance battery A.1-A.8, MCP safety boundary per muster PROTOCOLS.md 4.5 + fleet foreman-only rule + serve non-goals, auth story (loopback-only hard gate, serve.go:94). Full gate green on merged tree; Tier1 guard PASS on worktree commit.","foreman_note":"Decisions D1-D6 landed: D1 read-only surface; D2 served