 {"id":"DF-BOARDCTL-15","title":"P2 — skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md (v1.5.0) predates the two newest subcommands: sweep-status and install are absent from the agent-facing entry-points section","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T18:50:00+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"OBSERVED 2026-09-24 (dogfood run 15). The in-repo usage skill is what teaches future agents this CLI; its entry-points list stops at the pre-BT-054 surface — `sweep-status` (landed 2026-09-24, REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001) and `install` (board-lint pre-commit hook, BT-054) appear nowhere in the file, and the version pin stays 1.5.0. README.md DOES document sweep-status (line 251) but not install. An agent loading the skill would use validate --repair where sweep-status --apply is now the sanctioned write path, or would never learn the hook exists. FIX DIRECTION: bump the skill to 1.6.0: add both commands with their exit contracts (sweep-status exits 0 in BOTH modes — census is a finding, not a failure; install --dry-run prints the hook block), plus the run-15 verification results. Docs-only fix.","detail":{"fingerprint":"dg15-df-boardctl-15-skill-stale"},"complexity":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T23:35:47+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"1e09d45","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Wave worker glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm: skill-freshness gate (TestUsageSkillCoversEveryTopLevelCommand parses the real usageText constant — same string --help prints — and asserts every top-level command appears in Entry points OR Proven commands; gate caught real drift on first run: render/import/serve documented only in Report surface, now added, skill bumped 1.6.0->1.7.0; TestSkillCoverageParserProvesGatesBite pins the extractor to 16 commands; negative probes: sweep-status stripped / fake zz-newcmd both FAIL naming the missing command). Judge round 1 FAIL (criterion 3: header date unasserted) -> fixup worker wt/DF-BOARDCTL-15-fix: frontmatter date field + 45-day tolerance gate (TestUsageSkillDateWithinTolerance + TestUsageSkillDateGateBitesOnHeaderMutations; backdate probe 2026-06-01 FAILs at 115 days). Merged 4400ae4 + 7d53f8f, judge PASS round 2 (b897bb05).","foreman_note":"judge round 1 FAIL (criterion 3: header date not asserted, skill had no date field); fixup worker dispatched wt/DF-BOARDCTL-15-fix","completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":[],"worktree":"~/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-15","branch":"wt/DF-BOARDCTL-15"}
 {"id":"BT-064","title":"P2 — boardctl create GLUED a new row onto an unterminated last line, corrupting BOTH rows","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-25T13:09:05+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"appendBytes (internal/board/write.go) wrote straight through O_APPEND with no terminator check. Appending to a\nboard whose last line has no trailing newline put the new row on the SAME line: every line-based reader then sees\none malformed row ('Extra data' from any JSON parser) and BOTH ids disappear - silent data loss, no error, exit 0.\nObserved live on 2026-09-25: heading INT-CI-2693 landed glued to the row before it and had to be split back apart\nbyte-exact by hand (all 157 pre-existing lines verified unchanged afterwards).\nFixed: ensureTrailingNewline() normalizes the last byte before every append (absent/empty files untouched,\nterminated files byte-identical). Regression test internal/board/bt064_append_newline_test.go (RED before the fix:\n'want 2 lines, got 1 - the rows were glued'; GREEN after) plus the new-file and terminated-file edge cases.\nCommit 017577b, full suite green, binary installed and re-proven live: header + 2 rows on a deliberately\nunterminated file -> 3 lines, 3 parseable.","detail":{"fingerprint":"180f2e1bc40f086058ca847198be5beba6bd0e8660f158a7d8f5163f87ab68c9"},"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T13:09:05+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":"017577b","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"fixed in 017577b; RED->GREEN test + live proof on the installed binary","foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":[],"worktree":null,"branch":null}
 {"id":"BT-065","title":"P2 — boardctl Tier-1 guard was RED for everyone: the usage-skill date battery no-ops when the skill is stamped yesterday","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-25T13:09:05+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"cmd/boardctl/df15_skill_closure_test.go mutates the LIVE usage-skill frontmatter date. Its 'date one day old passes'\ncase sets the header to today-1; with skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md stamped 2026-09-24 that mutation was a NO-OP on\n2026-09-25, so the battery fataled ('the battery's date anchor has drifted') and go_tests failed - which blocks EVERY\ncommit to this repo at the Tier-1 guard, not just mine. Proven pre-existing: a pristine control worktree at origin/main\n(28b3ac0, 0 dirty files) failed identically.\nFixed the same way the neighbouring 'current date passes' case already documents: allowNoOp with an explicit reason -\nthe live body, asserted to pass its own gate at the top of the test, IS the one-day-old specimen when the stamp is\nyesterday. Semantics unchanged (all other cases still mutate and assert). Full suite 8/8 packages green. Commit 017577b.","detail":{"fingerprint":"d787f75514d7b3f2f18c0d398678bb5e479442b20cd949bea0642806835c8d60"},"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T13:09:05+00:00","capability_tags":[],"worker_status":"pending","commit_hash":"017577b","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"fixed in 017577b; RED->GREEN test + live proof on the installed binary","foreman_note":null,"completed_at":null,"sessions":null,"depends_on":[],"worktree":null,"branch":null}
